    "body": "## Summary\n\nDeepSeek-V4 passes `swiglu_limit=10` to its routed experts, but the Ascend runner only applies that limit for MX and block-FP8 kernels. BF16 and W8A8 INT8 fall through to plain SwiGLU, including the DeepEP/Ascend Ops branches. With gate=20 and up=20, the BF16 result is 400 instead of 100.\n\nUse the existing `NPUSwigluWithLimit` for the remaining weight formats when a limit is set. INT8 GMM2 already dynamically quantizes floating input when no per-token scale is supplied. Preserve the TP activation all-gather wrapper. The MX-specific branch and configurations without a limit keep their existing selection.\n\nThis covers the W8A8 DeepSeek-V4-Flash deployment documented for Ascend. The change is confined to the shared Ascend runner.\n\n## Validation\n\nOn Ascend, using the source-extracted runner, activation, quantization and grouped-matmul methods:\n\n- **16 compute checks passed:** BF16/INT8, cumulative/count group lists, all three transport selections with a clamp, and no-clamp controls for standard routing.\n- **2 graph replays passed:** BF16 and INT8 with changed inputs.\n- Five valid rows plus three NaN padding rows; valid outputs match a CPU clamp/SiLU reference followed by the same GMM2 path.\n- The standard-routing baseline fails all four clamped cases and passes all four no-clamp controls.\n- CPU selection checks cover 12 combinations, including unchanged MXFP4/block-FP8 selection, plus a simulated TP wrapper check.\n- Applicable lint checks pass; the two hooks requiring `python3` on Windows also pass when their scripts are invoked with `python`.\n\nThese checks execute real NPU ops, with transport selection scaffolded; they do not exercise distributed communication or full-model accuracy. An initial tiny-input run hit a device exception in the unchanged old DeepEP activation kernel, so the numerical baseline above is limited to standard routing. No throughput claim.\n\n[Harness and frozen sources](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/697ed4312c837e8f0dddc090512c5633b7f884f4/validate.py) · [NPU results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/697ed4312c837e8f0dddc090512c5633b7f884f4/RESULT_npu.json) · [CPU results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/697ed4312c837e8f0dddc090512c5633b7f884f4/RESULT_cpu.json)\n\nReport generated from the saved results:\n\n![NPU clamp validation](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/AkiYangDev/sglang@697ed4312c837e8f0dddc090512c5633b7f884f4/validation.png)\n\nRelated: #40438 handled the fused MX GMM1 path; this fixes the remaining BF16/INT8 activation selection. #47211 changes nearby runner setup but does not address this clamp.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41203804198](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41203804198)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41203804221](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41203804221)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41203804162](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41203804162)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
